EXTENSION "ARMDef_Magi_of_Hermes_PetalichusOfVerditius_Spells" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Magi of Hermes - Chapter Eleven: Petalichus of Verditus spells"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-08"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Magi_of_Hermes_Core_Ext"

    # The chapter's spells, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.

    #t395488232f6c82d0901504 ^"Unmake This Cloth" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 4, +1 Touch, +1 Herbam requisite)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Perdo"
            ^"Form" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 10
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Mom"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Herbam"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "PeAn(He) 10 R:Touch, D: Mom, T: Ind"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 99
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This spell unravels an item made of cloth, whether it be wool, linen, cotton, or silk. An Herbam casting requisite is required for for plant-based cloth.\n\nThe garment, tapestry, or other item is disassembled carefully with all knots undone and stitching unpicked.\n\nThe item is reduced to discrete piles of thread. A Dexterity + Finesse simple roll determines how orderly these piles are arranged and sorted.\n\n(Base 4, +1 Touch, +1 Herbam requisite)"
    }

    #tf09c41794cafa60f829b23 ^"Bind Fast" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 1, +2 Voice, +2 Group)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 5
            ^"Range" STRING "Voice"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Mom"
            ^"Target" STRING "Group"
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Herbam"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "ReAn(He) 5 R: Voice, D: Mom, T: Group"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 100
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The targets’ clothes seek out and bind themselves to the nearest other object, moving or not. If the members of a group are standing sufficiently close, this spell binds them together. The magic lasts just long enough for the clothes to bind themselves into knots, and then dissipates allowing the targets to free themselves by undoing or cutting the knotted cloth.\n\nWhile all of a target’s surface clothing will writhe and seek out something to bind to, there is no guarantee that all of it can. If the clothes are close-fitting, or there is not enough slack in the garment, the cloth will simply flail for a moment and then fall dormant. If there is sufficient cloth but there is nothing within its reach, the target may still become bound up as his clothes wrap and tie themselves around his limbs.\n\nAffected targets suffer a –3 penalty to all subsequent rolls for physical actions, but can free themselves by either dedicating a round to cutting or tearing the clothing, or by spending two rounds working to untie the knots.\n\nStoryguides may wish to give other options to particularly large, strong, or dexterous characters.\n\nUntil members of the target group have freed themselves, successive castings of this spell have no further effect.\n\n(Base 1, +2 Voice, +2 Group)"
    }

    #t35ea243b8c576b22b6020f ^"A Day’s Worth of Spinning" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 3, +1 Touch, +2 Group)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 10
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Mom"
            ^"Target" STRING "Group"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "ReAn 10 R:Touch, D: Mom, T: Group"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 100
        }
        DESCRIPTION "One of the first spells taught to Petalichus by his mater, this spell cleans, cards, and spins a whole fleece, or a bale of cotton or flax, into thread in a matter of moments. If dye is available when the spell is cast, the thread can be dyed as the caster directs. A Herbam casting requisite is required for plant-based cloth.\n\nThis is an Average task for a mundane spinner, so the caster must make a Perception + Finesse (precision) + stress die roll against an Ease Factor of 12 (Craft Ease Factor 9 + 3 for using Craft Magic).\n\nFailing the roll results in a badly spun fleece, probably with flecks of dirt still clinging to the thread. A botched roll ruins the fleece outright, though this may not be immediately apparent.\n\nSee *Covenants*, page 49 for more on Rego Craft Magic.\n\n(Base 3, +1 Touch, +2 Group)"
    }

    #t92a90433e77512eea19576 ^"A Day’s Worth of Weaving" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 3, +1 Touch, +2 Group)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 10
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Mom"
            ^"Target" STRING "Group"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "ReAn 10 R:Touch, D: Mom, T: Group"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 100
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This spell is exceptionally good at making simple cloth, but casters may find it difficult to create cloth of any great quality or highly patterned tapestries. The table below lists the base Ease Factors for weaving bolts of cloth in a single casting. Treat each bolt of cloth as being two paces in length by one pace wide. Successive castings can extend the current bolt of cloth rather than creating a new item. Members of Petalichus’ lineage have traditionally used this spell in practicing their Finesse.\n\nThe caster makes a Perception + Finesse (precision) + stress die and compares the result against the table below.\n\nCloth Bolt’s Level Craft Magic Quality Ease Factor Shoddy Trivial 6 Standard Simple 9 Superior Average 15 Excellent Hard 18\n\nIt is a harder task to create patterned cloth. A simple repeating pattern adds +3 to the Ease Factor, while an image or words woven into the cloth adds +6.\n\nSee *City & Guild*, page 67 for more on item quality. A Herbam casting requisite is required for work involving cotton or linen.\n\n(Base 3, +1 Touch, +2 Group)"
    }

    #t2fb7b3f70c8da5bda8f36f ^"The Even Hand of The Determined Weaver" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 1, +1 Touch, +1 Part, +1 for size, +1 for Creo requisite)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 5
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Mom"
            ^"Target" STRING "Part"
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "Re(Cr)An 5 R: Touch, D: Mom, T: Part"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 100
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Like The Weaver’s Subtle Art (below), this spell makes a lasting change to a tapestry or other item made from cloth (whether made from wool, cotton, silk, or linen).\n\nAny geometric shape or regular line in or on the item, or even the shape of the item itself, can be made even and precise. The Creo requisite ensures that the lines and shapes affected by this spell are perfect examples of their type.\n\nThis spell is used to enhance items, especially when making Excellent-quality wares, or Items of Quality as per the Verditius House Mystery detailed in *Houses of Hermes: Mystery Cults*, page 124.\n\nThe application of this spell alone is not enough to raise the true quality of an item (it cannot be made more hardy or more richly colored, for instance), but it is enough to aid spells that require certain mathematical resonances.\n\nThe individual changes made by the spell may stand out and draw the eye of those interested in the piece. Those looking at the work should make a Perception + Awareness + simple die roll against an Ease Factor of 9. On a success they notice the precision of the affected areas. Those who have the ability may substitute their Weaver craft ability for Awareness when making the check.\n\nA Herbam casting requisite is required for tapestries that include plant-based cloth or yarn.\n\n(Base 1, +1 Touch, +1 Part, +1 for size, +1 for Creo requisite)"
    }

    #tcd36637e06c142bd742a75 ^"The Treacherous Cloak" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 5
            ^"Range" STRING "Sight"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Conc"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "ReAn 5 R: Sight, D: Conc, T: Ind"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 100
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This spell uses a target’s clothes against him, twisting them into cords that then strangle the target for as long as the caster keeps concentrating.\n\nUsing the deprivation rules in **ArM5**, page 180, the target must make a Stamina check every 5 rounds. Additionally, the target can attempt a Strength + Athletics stress roll against the caster’s Dexterity + Finesse Simple roll in order to break the grip of the clothes. If the character is being helped, use the highest Strength + Athletics score and add 1 for each other person helping.\n\nThe target can attempt a Brave Personality Trait roll against an Ease Factor of 9 in order to perform an action other than attempting to free himself from the grip of his own clothes.\n\nThe caster must, as usual, succeed in Concentration rolls each round.\n\n(base 1, +3 Sight, +1 Concentration)"
    }

    #t56ca25eb0d4054f51f4c53 ^"The Weaver’s Subtle Art" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 1, +1 Touch, +1 Part, +1 for size, +1 for Finesse)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Animal"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 5
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Mom"
            ^"Target" STRING "Part"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "ReAn 5 R: Touch, D: Mom, T: Part"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 101
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This spell allows the caster to make minor alterations to a finished tapestry or embroidered item, such as changing a subject’s pose, improving a likeness, or rewording an embroidered phrase. The change is minor in relation to the whole, never making up more than a fraction of the item, but as this spell can act on large tapestries, the individual change may itself be quite large. The change retains the original character of the work, so the intrinsic workmanship cannot, in itself, be improved through this spell.\n\nThe version known to Petalichus was handed down through generations of his confraternity. Casters who know this version may use their Weaver craft ability in place of Finesse when determining the quality of the effect. Magi who invent this spell, or learn it from another source, use Finesse as normal.\n\nA Herbam casting requisite is required for tapestries using plant-based thread.\n\n(Base 1, +1 Touch, +1 Part, +1 for size, +1 for Finesse)"
    }

    #t1ed8f5561bd7d22457b3ff ^"Arachne’s Tuition" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Corpus"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 20
            ^"Range" STRING "Eye"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "ReCo 20 R:Eye, D: Sun, T: Ind"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 101
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Cast by a master on his apprentice, this spell allows the master to control the apprentice’s movements for a day.\n\nThe caster can suspend the spell, allowing the apprentice to continue with a task or exercise, and then resume control in order to help the apprentice through a particularly complex task or to correct his student and show how something should be done. The apprentice learns at a much deeper level by having his own actions controlled from within, rather than simply being guided from without.\n\nThis spell is designed to assist with the training of physical skills, notably craft skills. Each season a master uses this spell to instruct an apprentice, he can add 1 to his Training Source Quality (see **ArM5**, page 164).\n\nThis version was developed generations ago within Petallichus’ line of Verditius weavers, though others certainly exist elsewhere within House Verditius and perhaps also in other Houses.\n\nTwo seasons of using this spell on an apprentice counts as one year of being under a constant magical effect as per **ArM5**, page 168, and inflicts 1 Warping point in that year. (Base 4, +1 Eye, +2 Sun, +1 control over fine movements)"
    }

    #tc5b5c5ae32499bc371f8ab ^"Remain Within Those Walls" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Corpus"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 20
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Ring"
            ^"Target" STRING "Arcane"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "ReCo 20 R: Touch, D: Ring, T: Arcane"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 101
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Circle A variant on a warding theme, this spell cast with an Arcane Circle target both imprisons people within its bounds and prevents them from crossing into the Arcane Circle.\n\nThe Arcane Circle target is usable by those who know the Hermetic Geometry Mystery, and allows the caster to draw a circle at his location while calculating and casting against a sympathetically identical circle in a remote location (see *The Mysteries Revised Edition*, page 95).\n\nThose with Resistance (through Parma or Might) are not confined or restricted unless this spell Penetrates that resistance. Arcane Connections to a named target may be used in order to increase the Penetration as normal, though the increased Penetration is only valid against that named target.\n\nAs the base effect for warding spells is Touch, Ring, Circle, the Arcane Circle target raises the level of the spell by one magnitude as it is more complex than its mundane equivalent, but no modifier is required for either Touch or Ring.\n\n(base 15, +1 Arcane Circle)"
    }

    #te684f196d9615424d5f1c4 ^"To See As Though a Plethron Distant" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 2, +3 Sight, +1 Concentration, +3 Special target based on Room +1)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Intellego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Imaginem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 25
            ^"Range" STRING "Sight"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Conc"
            ^"Target" STRING "Special"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "InIm 25 R: Sight, D: Conc, T: Special"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 101
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This spell allows the caster to see and hear his surroundings as though he was standing in another place he can naturally see. The spell does not enhance the caster’s natural sight or hearing.\n\nThe caster has some freedom to move his vantage point, but cannot move into any place that he cannot naturally see from his physical location. Moving the viewpoint requires a Simple Stamina + Concentration Roll vs. Ease Factor 6.\n\nThe “plethron” of the spell title is a Greek measurement roughly equivalent to 100 feet, although the spell’s range allows for a potentially greater distance.\n\nPetalichus and his brother Cononites have investigated this spell, as Petalichus had anticipated that he would be able to use it to gain sight of new viable targets. This proved not to be the case. William Bonisagi theorized that the species, recreated as they are, bear insufficient connection to the things they represent to support casting spells against them. By being so far removed, the magus would essentially be attempting to cast his spells on mere apparitions.\n\nHowever, using this spell to aid with Hermetic Geometry spells (those using Arcane Line, Arcane Circle, and Arcane Ring) reduces the Distance Level by 1 if the caster can now see his target. This is cumulative with other spells or devices that may also reduce the Distance Level (see *The Worldly Halysis* later).\n\nThe Target is based on Room, but is more complex as it allows unbounded spaces to be targeted. Any area comparable to Room can be targeted.\n\n(Base 2, +3 Sight, +1 Concentration, +3 Special target based on Room +1)"
    }

    #t21a9ad46b65f6304303f2d ^"The Unwelcoming Room" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 4, +3 Line, +1 Concentration, +2 Room)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Form" STRING "Mentem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 30
            ^"Range" STRING "Line"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Conc"
            ^"Target" STRING "Room"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "CrMe 30 R: Line, D: Conc, T: Room"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 101
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Targeted on a distant room using the Arcane Line Range, this spell induces anger in all affected targets. A stress roll using an appropriate Personality Trait (like Calm or Restrained) against an Ease Factor of 9 is required to keep the anger under control. Aggressive traits (like Argumentative, Intolerant, or Angry) work against the roll. A failure inclines the target to aggressive action against anyone or anything that could appear or feel threatening.\n\nPetalichus knows the effect The Gift has on mundanes, and recognizes that the fear and distrust it fosters in them can easily be triggered into something more dangerous. Petalichus uses this spell to heighten tensions and use them against his enemies from a position of safety.\n\n(Base 4, +3 Line, +1 Concentration, +2 Room)"
    }

    #t2290c6f797cfa3a92559f3 ^"A Day’s Grace" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Vim"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 30
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Hours"
            ^"Target" STRING "Individual"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "ReVi 30 R: Touch D: Hours T: Individual"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 102
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Using this spell, the caster is able to suppress one other spell he casts at the same time as this spell for a Duration counted in Celestial Hours (see The Mysteries Revised Edition, page 49).\n\nThe suppressed spell can have a level up to 25 and may be Spontaneous, Ceremonial or Formulaic. Ritual spells are too complex to be suppressed by this spell although should a version of this spell be designed as a Ritual that should be possible.\n\nSpells with Circle and/or Ring Duration (including Arcane Circle and Arcane Ring) are also suppressed but fail if the circle inscribed during casting is broken before the spell is released (Arcane Circles and Rings are still visible to those with Second Sight, and may be broken by them before the spell is released).\n\nSight-Ranged spells must be targeted during the initial casting. Once the spell has been cast, the target will still be affected by it whether or not that target is still visible to the caster or not, though only where that target remains in the same location until the spell is triggered.\n\n(base 15, +1 Touch, +2 Hours - equivalent of Sun)"
    }

    #t1efd72e01660c765189c1b ^"Sense the Weight of Divine Power" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tM30boZOkiiaD5LRZZQQ1ymk ^"Formulaic Spell"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Spell Design" STRING "(Base 2, +1 Touch)"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Intellego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Vim"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 3
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Mom"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Printed Stat Line" STRING "InVi 3 R: Touch, D: Mom, T: Ind"
            ^"Source" STRING "Magi of Hermes"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 102
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This rote (designed using the Hermetic Numerology Mystery Virtue) is a simple effect to tell the caster what strength of Divine aura he is currently standing in.\n\nPetalichus has three other rotes that each perform the same effect for one of the other three Realms.\n\n(Base 2, +1 Touch)"
    }

